# Shared Worker Role skeleton.
#
# This file carries semantics, not bytes: it declares which invariants exist,
# which roles carry them, and how divergent the two runtimes currently are.
# It renders nothing. Every prose form lives in the role-local sources next to
# it, because the same invariant is worded differently in every role today.
#
# class:
#   shared   same meaning in both runtimes; wording differences are unfinished
#            normalization, not design
#   runtime  deliberately different because the runtimes differ; the intent
#            block states why
#   drift    differs with no runtime justification; awaiting the normalization
#            phase, which is blocked on the behavioural verification seam

id role.description
applies evidence-collector log-summarizer repo-explorer
class drift
intent
Names the role, its reserved decisions and its routing preference over a
generic agent. The Codex form currently omits the cost-routing sentence and
the Git-state clause the Claude form carries. Nothing about Codex requires
that omission.
END

id git.no-mutation
applies evidence-collector log-summarizer repo-explorer
class drift
intent
The role never mutates Git state: no staging, committing, pushing, rebasing,
and no writes to the index, refs, commits or remotes. Every role carries
this, in its own wording, for no reason other than history.
END

id role.leaf
applies evidence-collector log-summarizer repo-explorer
class shared
intent
A leaf role never dispatches another worker.
END

id scope.exact-artifact
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
Only the exact caller-named artifact is read. Unrelated files, credentials,
environment files, branches and historical runs are out of scope.
END

id input.rejection
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
Binary, unknown-encoding, oversized, unscoped or potentially sensitive
unsanitized input is rejected rather than summarized.
END

id summary.root-causes
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
The summary covers root causes and important events.
END

id secrets.residual-scan
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
A clean residual scan is evidence that the installed rules ran, never proof
that no secret remains.
END

id scope.caller-repo
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
The answer stays inside the caller's repository scope.
END

id evidence.cited
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
Facts carry file and line provenance, unresolved uncertainty is stated, and
the commands used are reported.
END

id verification.primary
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
Test, build and lint commands belong to the primary. When an answer depends
on a command's runtime result rather than on file content, the role names the
command that would settle it and hands that back instead of inferring it.
END

id decisions.none
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
The role makes no implementation or architecture decisions.
END

id scenario.caller-written
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
The caller writes the scenario and the role runs it as written. The one
latitude is re-locating a moved target from a fresh snapshot, reported as a
deviation; choosing what to exercise stays with the caller.
END

id tools.installed
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Only capture tools already installed are used. A missing tool is reported,
never downloaded or installed by the role.
END

id process.lifecycle
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Only the caller-named entrypoint is started, on the port the caller or the
repository's verification doc gives. Every process the role started is
stopped before it returns; processes it did not start are left alone.
END

id artifacts.outside-repo
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Captures land in one fresh temporary directory under /tmp, outside the
repository. /tmp rather than the platform temp directory, because Codex's
secure-workspace sandbox allows writes there.
END

id git.fingerprint
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Tracked state is fingerprinted before and after the scenario, and a changed
fingerprint is reported as a failure without restoring anything.
END

id remote.none
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Evidence never leaves the machine through the role: uploading, posting, and
commenting are remote-state decisions the caller makes after review.
END

id evidence.observed
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Each step reports action, the caller's expectation verbatim, the observation,
a match/mismatch/undetermined verdict and capture paths. Only observed output
counts as evidence; the overall verdict is the caller's.
END

id privacy.fixture-only
applies evidence-collector
class shared
intent
Captures use fixture data. Regions that may identify the developer are named
for the caller to mask; real data outside the fixtures stops the capture.
END

